#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4791998a-2e12-50fa-8127-8fe3482a030d" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Maclaurin Series of a Function in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41b0841b-441a-591d-aca8-6116a1a6ff60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-x}={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2n}}{n!}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251107} {:answer/id #uuid "6f0edabb-4065-5d29-9f5a-18d483a10bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-x}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{n}}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251465} {:answer/id #uuid "74ec68e5-d2c3-5ec0-ba78-35a236574b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+x}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251522} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9d690c-d695-5b0f-b8eb-02dc85f4db9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-x}={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-1)^{n}{x}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251746} {:answer/id #uuid "ec08d2c2-ee7b-5dce-9a0f-8ee791bf6430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-x}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{x}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec08d2c2-ee7b-5dce-9a0f-8ee791bf6430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-x}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{x}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252627} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f1980d2-38d2-5829-9bb3-9cb9f8b1dada" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "408262f2-3790-57f2-9454-49ad6b184b07" :question/math-academy-id "q-11715" :question/problem "Express the Maclaurin series expansion for $\\frac{1}{1-x},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{1-x}=1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯\\,,\\,x\\in (-1,1)\n$$\n\nusing sigma notation." :question/worked-solution "The first four terms of the series are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =1 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =x \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can express these terms using a common format, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={x}^{0} \\\\ {a}_{1} & ={x}^{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe deduce that the general formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{x}^{n}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096658 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Scalar Factors in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e5ae413-be1a-5211-ad08-178e5e19be0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e5ae413-be1a-5211-ad08-178e5e19be0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291113} :answer-field/id #uuid "2daa9284-83e4-5449-8185-db49a6c674e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d709123-c548-51c1-96cd-bc8ac660e378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d709123-c548-51c1-96cd-bc8ac660e378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291242} :answer-field/id #uuid "956ba8d7-fa47-5f7a-b145-9f5e1da669dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d447ec6b-433a-5b79-9c9d-143f856c643d" :question/math-academy-id "q-275128" :question/problem "![](images/99/992be4e67316804381ffc38860d2eaf23fd4a93cfe22ec4918c30c41e34ade57.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/c0/c0f7f4df52373ca602aff41c97a5b8413f510353874540b76147c527a2f4b18c.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=\\frac{1}{2}|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $r$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-\\frac{1}{2}r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=\\frac{5}{2}|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-\\frac{5}{2}s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}r-\\frac{5}{2}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=-\\frac{1}{2}r-\\frac{5}{2}s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu =-\\frac{5}{2}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152185 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Point Under a Linear Transformation of a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f02332b-f7b0-5a90-b31e-e4497deecef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f02332b-f7b0-5a90-b31e-e4497deecef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293066} :answer-field/id #uuid "81cae86e-00f7-5e39-a493-45075afd382e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3ea1a52-6f26-5d94-9a72-67e3369860f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3ea1a52-6f26-5d94-9a72-67e3369860f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293700} :answer-field/id #uuid "df8b593e-096b-5b7d-acf1-efb2222d37c9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c22179b9-c0f6-5d75-8b5d-9beb46bf3a76" :question/math-academy-id "q-281092" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${Y}^{′}$, the image of $Y(-2,-3)$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${Y}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $Y$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $Y:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${Y}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${Y}^{′}(-2,11).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d14dbef-9a16-537e-a182-87fd6853e543" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Divergent Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dedfdfd-8dd2-59cb-8d39-a5f814fc80d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096037} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea24cf9-633b-5633-bb0d-df5b3f044f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096038} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ae7a67-8a5a-5ed6-9305-f30e1d7e6df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096039} {:answer/id #uuid "be663b18-395d-5370-85ab-9dd35b89f7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096040} {:answer/id #uuid "e88cd036-c103-52c6-a10e-c0be5a669dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096041}] :answer-field/id #uuid "84e15014-b2fa-554e-9a80-0ae44d96b0a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096036}] :question/id #uuid "e58cf1f9-7d5e-58f7-92b0-62318a7f3320" :question/math-academy-id "q-74054" :question/problem "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\n1. $a_{n} = \\frac{n^{3} - 1}{n^{2} + 1}$ for $n \\ge 1$\n2. $a_{n} = \\frac{n^{5} - n}{n^{4} - 2}$ for $n \\ge 1$\n3. $a_{n} = \\frac{1}{n^{2} + 8}$ for $n \\ge 1$"}]}
